<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <changeSet id="002-batch-metadata-mit" author="dcre">
        <!-- A-81: the sqlFile gained IF NOT EXISTS on every CREATE, which CHANGES this
             changeset's checksum and would fail validation on every database that had
             already executed it ("was: 9:6745... but is now: 9:fcef..."), observed live on
             MRR. Liquibase's documented escape hatch is the right one here rather than a
             new id per service: the content is autogenerated framework DDL whose integrity
             is now guaranteed by the IF NOT EXISTS clauses themselves, so re-running it
             cannot damage a database in any state. Applying it is what must stay possible;
             the byte-for-byte checksum is not the control that matters for this file. -->
        <validCheckSum>ANY</validCheckSum>
        <!-- SCRUM-107 (MIS->MIT rename): the id and the sqlFile path both changed, and
             mis_databasechangelog was renamed to mit_databasechangelog, so against any
             database migrated under the old names this changeset is NEW and would re-run
             its CREATE TABLEs. Every other changeset in this service is already MARK_RAN
             guarded; this one was the sole unguarded changeset.

             A-81 (2026-08-07): the MARK_RAN precondition that guarded it is REMOVED. It
             tested ONE table out of the nine objects the sqlFile creates, so a pod killed
             mid-file left the tables present and the sequences absent, and the re-run read
             the surviving table as "already applied" and skipped the rest FOREVER. Observed
             live: mas_batch_job_instance_seq missing while all four tables existed, MAS
             failing every attempt. Idempotency now lives in the .sql itself (IF NOT EXISTS
             on every CREATE), which converges from a half-applied state instead of
             declaring it finished. -->
        <!-- LIQUIBASE-SQL-EXCEPTION: the Spring Batch 6.0.4 metadata schema is the
             framework's own autogenerated DDL (MIT_BATCH_ prefixed, EXIT_MESSAGE
             widened to TEXT for CockroachDB); it is shipped verbatim as an external
             .sql and cannot be re-expressed as typed Liquibase tags. Same pattern as
             every DCRE stage service (crr/ctv/mrr/mrv batch-metadata-<svc>.sql). -->
        <sqlFile path="db/changelog/2026/07/batch-metadata-mit.sql" splitStatements="true"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
